==Battleground==
*5 [[Znache]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Celeboodle]] (800%) spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[Celeboodle]] (800%) spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Celeboodle]] (800%) spawns after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>.
*1 [[Celeboodle]] (800%) spawns after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Celeboodle]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Znache]]s spawn, delay 30~50 seconds<sup>900f~1,500f</sup>.
**4 [[Dagshund]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**3 [[Zang Roo]]s spawn, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
**2 [[Cadaver Bear]]s spawn, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
If you brought a Zombie-focused lineup that can beat [[Big Peng Z Strikes/Wandering Lv.1~20|Wandering Lv.11+]] with the [[Ototo Corps|Holy Blast]] specifically, then you should be good. You should optimally already have a good [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|Anti-Zombie attacker]] that can outrange Cadaver Bear, though [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] works provided a good stepping stone. Just be sure to avoid hitting the base before the Holy Blast is fully charged so that you can immediately unburrow the Cadaver Bear. After dealing with the first Cadaver Bear, you should focus on rushing the base down. If the second Cadaver Bear does have time to spawn in, you should avoid unburrowing him with the Holy Blast so that your stack keeps destroying the base.

